-- title:
--   Inertia displacements at p ‖ M: ⟨ d₁⟩ Frobₚ = p Uₚ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero modulus $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$, with $M/p$ nonzero, and assume the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` (the series $q^{-1}$ times the integral power series `jNum`) lies in the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. Let $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$ index the excluded primes of the Hecke generator type. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit in $A$, whose residue field has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed; let $\varphi$ be a $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and acting on the residue field by $x \mapsto x^p$, and let $\sigma$ be an automorphism coming from the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $z$ be a point of $J_H = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, killed by some $n$ with $p \nmid n$, and let $d_1 \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ reduce to $p$ in $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$. Then the diamond endomorphism `diamondHBar M H d₁` applied to $\varphi \cdot (\sigma z - z)$ equals $p$ times the Hecke endomorphism `heckeOperatorHAlong` at $p$ applied to $\sigma z - z$.
--
--   This is Ribet's comparison, at a place above a prime $p$ exactly dividing the level, between the action of an arithmetic Frobenius twisted by a diamond operator and $p$ times $U_p$ on inertia displacements of prime-to-$p$ torsion; it rests on the description of the toric part of the Néron model of $J_H$ in terms of node units on the Deligne–Rapoport special fibre. It is used to deduce the corresponding identity on $J_1$, via [`ModularCurve.JOne.diamondOneBar_smul_pullbackAlongHom_smul_sub_self_eq_smul_heckeOperatorOneBar_of_isFrobeniusAt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JOne.diamondOneBar_smul_pullbackAlongHom_smul_sub_self_eq_smul_heckeOperatorOneBar_of_isFrobeniusAt).
